(1803442, 245962, 30817, '<td valign="top">I like the literal-thought-turned-into-a-photograph style of theme interpretation that you utilized.  That is an excellent training tool for representative photography.  You need to follow that up, however, with compositional considerations of equal importance to the process in order to claim success. Bricks (because of their chaotic linear nature) rarely make a good background, unless very, very out of focus.  The strong lighting and harsh shadow introduced by a single flash can almost never compliment skintones.  For people portraits, consider shaded outdoor lighting or using a white bounce card on the opposite side of the model from a window through which pours diffused sunlight. If skintones still are a problem, convert to B&amp;W which is nearly always more kind to skin.  Put your creativity for theme ideas into the art of photography and we will witness another bright light at this website.  6</td>', 'I like the literal-thought-turned-into-a-photograph style of theme interpretation that you utilized.  That is an excellent training tool for representative photography.  You need to follow that up, however, with compositional considerations of equal importance to the process in order to claim success. Bricks (because of their chaotic linear nature) rarely make a good background, unless very, very out of focus.  The strong lighting and harsh shadow introduced by a single flash can almost never compliment skintones.  For people portraits, consider shaded outdoor lighting or using a white bounce card on the opposite side of the model from a window through which pours diffused sunlight. If skintones still are a problem, convert to B&W which is nearly always more kind to skin.  Put your creativity for theme ideas into the art of photography and we will witness another bright light at this website.  6', '2005-10-22 17:42:42.000000', NULL, 1),
