(1812996, 245950, 33068, '<td valign="top">I was totally bummed when I got home from vacation to find out that I had been disqualified.  I know it''s my fault for not paying closer attention to the submission rules but still disappointed nonetheless.  It was doing better than my other two challenge entries.  &lt;sigh&gt;<br/> <br/>Anyway, I''m guessing they requested validation because the picture looks dodged and burned.  The fog effect was created by running the picture through neat image three times.  The original image had a lot of noise.  It would have been perfect for the grain entry in its original state.  The only other processing I used was channel mixer, auto levels, and auto contrast.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-26 00:54:20.</i></td>', 'I was totally bummed when I got home from vacation to find out that I had been disqualified.  I know it''s my fault for not paying closer attention to the submission rules but still disappointed nonetheless.  It was doing better than my other two challenge entries.  <sigh> Anyway, I''m guessing they requested validation because the picture looks dodged and burned.  The fog effect was created by running the picture through neat image three times.  The original image had a lot of noise.  It would have been perfect for the grain entry in its original state.  The only other processing I used was channel mixer, auto levels, and auto contrast.', '2005-10-26 01:45:08.000000', '2005-10-26 01:54:20.000000', 0),
