(1814287, 245901, 18219, '<td valign="top">Thank you very much for my red ribbon.<br/>I nearly have a complete collection now.<br/>Just the brown to go :-)<br/> <br/>Everyone always writes something profound and meaningful here after the challenge is over.<br/>So here is my attempt at it.<br/>We (actually my girlfriend Judi) rescued this dog (Rockett is her name) from the SPCA about ten months ago.<br/>She had been there about six weeks and probably didn''t have long left.<br/>We were told that she was half pit bull and half pointer and that was probably why nobody wanted her.<br/>But she is so loving and cuddly and sweet.<br/>OK, she may want to kill the squirrels in our garden, but that''s about it.<br/>We also have four cats and she hasn''t hurt them.<br/>Occasionally she can get defensive towards her food, but so can all animals.<br/>Pit bulls have got a bad name and it isnt justified.<br/> <br/>This <a href="//www.pbrc.net/info.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">website</a> is very informative if you are interested.<br/>A quote from their front page: <br/> <br/><b>Dogs considered "pit bulls" carry many stereotypes. Any time one of these dogs does something bad, the media makes sure we all know about it. The public never learns about the thousands of "pit bulls" that are cherished family pets, who are gentle with children and excel in obedience.</b> <br/> <br/>Oh yeah, in the picture I didnt actually say walkies,  I was promising her a greenie (a dental dog treat that she loves)<br/></td>', 'Thank you very much for my red ribbon.I nearly have a complete collection now.Just the brown to go :-) Everyone always writes something profound and meaningful here after the challenge is over.So here is my attempt at it.We (actually my girlfriend Judi) rescued this dog (Rockett is her name) from the SPCA about ten months ago.She had been there about six weeks and probably didn''t have long left.We were told that she was half pit bull and half pointer and that was probably why nobody wanted her.But she is so loving and cuddly and sweet.OK, she may want to kill the squirrels in our garden, but that''s about it.We also have four cats and she hasn''t hurt them.Occasionally she can get defensive towards her food, but so can all animals.Pit bulls have got a bad name and it isnt justified. This website is very informative if you are interested.A quote from their front page:  Dogs considered "pit bulls" carry many stereotypes. Any time one of these dogs does something bad, the media makes sure we all know about it. The public never learns about the thousands of "pit bulls" that are cherished family pets, who are gentle with children and excel in obedience.  Oh yeah, in the picture I didnt actually say walkies,  I was promising her a greenie (a dental dog treat that she loves)', '2005-10-26 11:36:45.000000', NULL, 0),
