(1817006, 246438, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Great shot for the "What" category.  If you hadn''t given it the title that you did I would have sat and wondered for quite a while what the image was of.  Probably coming up with the idea of some funky cheerios.  I love the perspective you took, above always gives a different take o a subject. I think you were nice and outside the box on this one.  I do like the coloring, placement as well as the composition of the shot.  The image feels deep by using a subject that has some length to look down.  I really like that you left it at and odd number and nothing was even placed.  The depth of the shoots themselves on the top is also another great feature. Great job, the only thing I would possibly change, which you probably had no control over were the small specks mainly on the left side.</td>', '*Critique Club* Great shot for the "What" category.  If you hadn''t given it the title that you did I would have sat and wondered for quite a while what the image was of.  Probably coming up with the idea of some funky cheerios.  I love the perspective you took, above always gives a different take o a subject. I think you were nice and outside the box on this one.  I do like the coloring, placement as well as the composition of the shot.  The image feels deep by using a subject that has some length to look down.  I really like that you left it at and odd number and nothing was even placed.  The depth of the shoots themselves on the top is also another great feature. Great job, the only thing I would possibly change, which you probably had no control over were the small specks mainly on the left side.', '2005-10-27 01:27:42.000000', NULL, 0);
